35.3.5 Dwarfish racial ascension - dwarf selected as the race, did
  not weild a non-dwarfish weapon (only dwarfish mattock, dwarvish
  short sword, or dwarvish spear allowed), did not wear non-dwarfish
  armor (only dwarvish mithril, dwarvish cloak, dwarvish iron helm,
  dwarvish roundshield, and iron shoes allowed). (Yes, iron shoes do
  not say "Dwarvish", but who else do you see generated wearing them?)
  Patience: Slight  Luck: Slight  Planning: Trivial

Dwarfie Notes

Dwarves: Well, you can find a fair amount of dwarvish armor
(mithril, cloak, shield, helm) and there are dwarvish weapons
(short sword, spear, mattock). Archeologist could be a natural
choice, but I am trying to simultaneously do all of the racial
ascensions, and I already picked Arch. for the Gnome. So, a
good second choice for a dwarf? Caveman. Why? If I am going
to take advantage of all the dwarvish armor available, spell
failure rate is going to be very close to 100%. So, I might
as well go as a combat-wombat. Also, the Quest artifact
supplies the always-nice magic resistance and it only has
to be carried to do it (no weilding or wearing required).

Attempt #1: killed by a xorn
Attempt #2: killed by a kobold
Attempt #3: killed by a giant bat
Attempt #4: killed by a homunculus

Attempt #5:
T5 I've removed the starting leather armor and weilded nothing.
T1676 I made it to Minetown, although it was via a level
teleport trap that left my dog two levels up. I had enough
money for one donation (still Elvl 1) and got four points.
That, combined with a +2 ring of protection I found gives
an AC of 4. Not too bad considering I'm still naked.
T1888 Found some dwarvish mithril on my way back to my dog.
I immediately put it on. Cursed and -1, but oh well. It still
gives me 5 points of AC and three star magic cancellation.
T6506 Wow. A 6 by 8 hardware store on Dlvl 9, one below the
Oracle. No magic whistle though. Bummer.
T10279 I've completed Sokoban (for the bag, not the amulet
that I was hoping for). I'm at AC -4 and have been fighting
everything bare-handed as no dwarish weapons have turned up
yet. (So, yes, I did beat feet when I saw a chicktrice
appear on the top level of Sokoban).
T17258 Finally got a magic whistle to keep my (now) large
dog and Elf Lord close. Still no dwarvish weapons. I am
Expert in Bare Handed now.
T19413 Finally found a dwarvish short sword exploring the
lower levels of the Mines with my White Dragon and mumak.
T19612 Sigh. A poly trap in the Mines changed me to a
wumpus and broke the mithril. I haven't found a backup
suit of it yet either.
T22477 Well, I found another dwarf that had basically one
of everything dwarfish (other than a spear). I used the
short sword for a while and noticed I was not getting a
chance to improve. Checking up on Caveman shows that of
the three dwarvish weapons, the short sword will be stuck
at unskilled, mattock could get to basic, spear could get
to basic. Hmm... time to switch to the mattock.
T29669 Continued play, main stash on Dlvl 18, naked AC 0,
mattock is now +7, some enchantment on armor.
T31772 Dlvl 22 was Medusa. Still no amulet of reflection,
but I am taunted with the Perseus statue holding a sheild
of reflection.
T32442 Dlvl 25 is the Castle (I descend to it with a
blessed scroll of genocide in my hand and a lightning
wand ready to engrave.)
T34626 I've cleared the front of the Castle and got the
wand. I think I'll try the simple, sure route:
T34627 Wish #1 from the castle wand: 3 b?SoC (got 1).
T34628 Wish #2 from the castle wand: blessed amulet of
reflection.
T37886 Cleared the Fort (partially for the gold, partially
for the experience to get to level 14). Processed the
gold through the last priest in the normal dungeon
(Dlvl 24) and got another point of AC. Now AC -2 naked,
-19 with armor. (Yeah, I'll eventually get/wish for
a magic marker and get it lower.)
T44716 Did the fort and just finished the Quest. Currently
I have a Water Troll pet. It is basically time to review
and prepare for the lower depths.
T46123 And I lose the Troll to a Trapper.
T46264 Attempting more wishes shows the wand must have
been at 0:2. So, lets charge it.
T46267 Wish #3 from the castle wand: magic marker.
T46293 Wish #4 from the castle wand: magic marker.
T46326 I'm going to save myself some hassle. So, I write
some genocide scrolls and...
T46334 Goodbye L
T46335 Goodbye ;
T46336 Goodbye t
T46337 Goodbye w
T46338 Goodbye R
T46340 Wish #5 from the castle wand: blessed figurine of
an Archon.
T47279 I get around to applying the figurine and the Archon
(now named Sunny Boy) who came with Sunsword.
T58013 I've explored down to the vibrating square and am
doing final preparations for an ascension run. I used alchemy
to make 5 potions of gain level and let the pet Archon quaff
them. It is now level 33. That will be enough to tackle the
Wizard the first 5 times he shows (if I understand the game
correctly).
I have a wrestable wish left. What to use it for? Another
Archon? I think I'll just try for two more gain levels for
my current one.
T58401 Wish #7 from the castle wand 2b?oGL.
T61813 OK, I think this character is ready for the ascension
run. He could use two more points of strength, but otherwise
is pretty well-prepared. I think I'll break here and try
to get one of the other racial characters moving along.



